# Git commit message format (English)

Write **commit titles and bodies in English**. Do not use the Chinese `模块：` subject style unless the user explicitly asks for it.

## Subject line (first line)

Use **[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/)** style:

```text
type(scope): short imperative description
```

- **type**: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `build`, `test`, etc.
- **scope** (optional): area, e.g. `ui`, `sensor`, `storage`, `oled`, `rtos`.
- **description**: imperative mood, no period at the end, **~50 characters or fewer** when possible.

Examples:

```text
feat(ui): unify long-press entry and double-click exit
fix(sensor): correct FIFO watermark after mode switch
refactor(gesture): extract gesture_post_event helper
```

## Line breaks and body

- After the subject line, add a **blank line**, then the **body** (one or more paragraphs).
- Do not cram the body on the same line as the subject.
- Wrap body lines at about **72 characters** when a line would get too long.

## Good example

```text
feat(ui): unify long-press entry and double-click exit

Extract gesture_post_event for queue sends. Add sensor_raw_to_mg for
FIFO samples. Align storage-ready gating with menu registration.
```

## Bad examples

Single line mixing subject and body:

```text
feat(ui): unify long-press entry and double-click exit Extract gesture_post_event for queue sends.
```

Non-English subject (unless user requested Chinese):

```text
UI模块：统一长按进入与双击退出交互
```
